# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Code coverage profiles and other test artifacts
*.out
coverage.*
*.coverprofile
profile.cov

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# Go workspace file
go.work
go.work.sum

# env file
.env

# Editor/IDE
# .idea/
# .vscode/

# Dashboard toolchain. dashboard/dist is committed on purpose: dashboard/embed.go
# embeds it, so `go build` alone produces a binary that serves the dashboard.
dashboard/node_modules/
dashboard/.env

# Local build output and databases. dist/ is anchored to the repository root: the
# release workflow builds there, while dashboard/dist is committed and must not match.
bin/
/dist/
data/
